hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15821","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Said ibn al-Mualla, he said: I was praying and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me and called me, but I did not come to him until I had prayed, then I came to him. He said: What prevented you from coming to me? He said: I said, I was praying. He said: Did not Allah, Blessed and Exalted, say: O you who believe, respond to Allah and to the Messenger when he calls you to that which gives you life. Then he said: Shall I not teach you the greatest surah in the Quran before I leave the mosque? He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to leave, so I reminded him, and he said: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; it is the seven oft-repeated and the mighty Quran which I have been given."
